{
    "background_story": "Jamie was a renowned Shakespearean actor, celebrated for his haunting portrayal of Macbeth on stage. His performances were always met with critical acclaim, as he brought a depth and nuance to the character that few others could match. But Jamie's fascination with the Scottish king went beyond the stage. He became obsessed with the themes of ambition, power, and the supernatural that drove Macbeth's tragic downfall. As he delved deeper into the play's psychology, Jamie began to see parallels between Macbeth's struggles and his own. He started to question the true cost of his own ambition, and the lengths to which he would go to achieve success. Jamie's exploration of Macbeth's psyche became a personal journey, one that blurred the lines between reality and the world of the play.",
